{"sys":{"type":"Array"},"total":1,"skip":0,"limit":100,"items":[{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"2A67N47ntcdQbKhHOd7GdD","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T11:26:54.784Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T11:26:57.168Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":47,"revision":2,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"article"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"EXPLAINED: What is F1’s ‘ADUO’ engine upgrade system – and how will it work?","slug":"explained-what-is-f1s-aduo-engine-upgrade-system-and-how-will-it-work","seoTitle":"EXPLAINED: What is F1’s ‘ADUO’ engine upgrade system – and how will it work?","displayTitle":"What is F1’s ‘ADUO’ engine upgrade system?","socialShareTitle":"What is F1’s ‘ADUO’ engine upgrade system?","metaDescription":"To encourage close competition, F1’s Technical Regulations for 2026 and beyond will allow manufacturers to make updates to their homologated power units – in specific situations – under a new development mechanism. But what is the so-called ‘ADUO’, and how does it work? F1.com presents an all-in-one explainer… ","abstract":"F1.com runs through a new development mechanism available to power unit manufacturers from the 2026 season.","socialShareImage":[{"url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png","bytes":2506639,"width":1920,"format":"png","height":1080,"metadata":{},"public_id":"fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png","resource_type":"image","access_control":[],"raw_transformation":"t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png"}],"leadsourceType":"Article","articleLocale":"en","articleType":"Feature","isExclusiveArticle":false,"heroArea":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"gcHCKtbNX629KdCSY2XPu"}},"body":[{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6YZVPYhcpLrR4UQbUdGYdH"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6R2KAXCj7KDHit9OS6hUJU"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"5HjuvBlAV6KU3jYRlLpqmM"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6eaThB0d95QskxG0dorESn"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"bOFt8MODvtMlcBUwlivWO"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"4RT8I3oKCVNLHtc1xiVHaW"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"3kifEXjDx6qSOmTIfJCsov"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"4DQlu3sQDLvb9i9VP95HkX"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6m5BWuGDLxEGhWtxOg0NYt"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6qBZcSw2hYcqZlfI2hONLL"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6kcKCnijMM4BSWAShaNVid"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"2QdCUJ2TfWbmULBleXtwcN"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"6IRygB5qY6mpYOp2Kgvou2"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"2zC5YIcs1oy8MlHHmICMrO"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"3NF3lo7axsfEs2vMHQAnEs"}}],"displayPrimaryTag":false,"articleTags":[{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"3MCJ3owpZpby8mcOoUVtIi"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"2Rkcy0QqWsqog4gsi6mQ2C"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"55LpDLkFiOGZ7W2byMrm5g"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"5TppklcnBMKv6j5ccPjaaa"}}],"darkModeOnly":false,"publicationChannel":[{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"2LGJVtZuDqTiFoQAbfh9Oz"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"3mFrXX2FHaESyGiwus8Ys4"}},{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Entry","id":"4Z3WmbMNskwsKWg84OwWUG"}}],"customPublishedAt":"2026-05-18T11:26:54.784Z"}}],"includes":{"Entry":[{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"2LGJVtZuDqTiFoQAbfh9Oz","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2023-04-25T14:23:01.179Z","updatedAt":"2023-11-09T14:48:03.903Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":6,"revision":3,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"channel"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"channelName":"Apple News"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"2QdCUJ2TfWbmULBleXtwcN","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:38:25.358Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-15T14:38:25.358Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":4,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 7","richTextBlock":"### What about F1’s cost cap?\n\nSince 2021, teams’ annual spends have been controlled under [the F1 cost cap](https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/explained-what-is-the-f1-cost-cap-and-why-has-it-gone-up.2tYtDIe5SbE5utjThctBT3).\n\nAs such, questions have arisen over how the ADUO will work under such restrictions – but FIA Single Seater Director Nikolas Tombazis moved to allay concerns.\n\n“It’s important to make clear that ADUO is not a kind of balance of performance mechanism,” he commented. “A team or manufacturer will not suddenly get greater fuel flow rate or more or less ballast.\n\n“It is, in fact, a cost cap relief mechanism, where a PU manufacturer meeting ADUO criteria during a review period is given an opportunity to develop its engine through a downward adjustment."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"2Rkcy0QqWsqog4gsi6mQ2C","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2018-04-24T16:59:36.541Z","updatedAt":"2023-03-08T05:26:48.983Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":16,"revision":5,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"tag"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"tagName":"FIA","tagDescription":"Current and breaking F1 FIA stories. Your go-to source for Formula 1 news, highlights, results, and expert commentary.","seoTitle":"FIA News and Videos | Formula 1","slug":"fia","tagGroup":"Content - Subject","tagImage":[{"url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Tag%20collections/Other/FIA.jpg","format":"jpg","metadata":{"alt_text":"FIA.jpg","caption":"FIA.jpg"},"public_id":"content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Tag%20collections/Other/FIA","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Tag%20collections/Other/FIA.jpg","resource_type":"image","raw_transformation":"f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Tag%20collections/Other/FIA.jpg"}]}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"2zC5YIcs1oy8MlHHmICMrO","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:38:50.984Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T11:09:42.093Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":11,"revision":3,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 8","richTextBlock":"“That’s not to underestimate it, but a manufacturer will still need to make the best engine in order to win. It’s not a magic bullet, or like the FIA is handing out brownie points to somebody who’s behind. It simply provides them with leeway to develop their power unit within the framework laid out by the Technical Regulations.”\n\nArticle E4.1.1.t of the 2026 Formula 1 Regulations sets out the positive impacts of the ADUO on power unit manufacturers’ expenditure.\n\nEvery manufacturer sitting 2-4% behind will get allowances up to USD $3.0 million; from 4-6% behind they will get up to USD $4.65m; from 6-8% they will get up to USD $6.35m; and from 8%-10% they will get up to USD $8m.\n\nManufacturers with a deficit of 10% or more will get an allowance for each ADUO period of up to USD $11m and, in 2026 only, further support might be offered."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"3MCJ3owpZpby8mcOoUVtIi","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2025-06-12T10:03:48.442Z","updatedAt":"2025-06-13T14:23:16.492Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":6,"revision":2,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"tag"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"tagName":"Explained","tagDescription":"Current and breaking Explained F1 stories. Your go-to source for Formula 1 news, podcasts, highlights, results, and expert commentary.","seoTitle":"Explained, News and Videos | Formula 1","slug":"explained","tagGroup":"Content - Subject","tagImage":[{"format":"png","width":1920,"height":1080,"public_id":"fom-website/2025/Miscellaneous/2025-start-barcelona","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1749481747/fom-website/2025/Miscellaneous/2025-start-barcelona.png","resource_type":"image","metadata":{},"access_control":[],"original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1749481747/fom-website/2025/Miscellaneous/2025-start-barcelona.png","url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1749481747/fom-website/2025/Miscellaneous/2025-start-barcelona.png","raw_transformation":"f_auto/q_auto"}]}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"3NF3lo7axsfEs2vMHQAnEs","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2024-10-30T09:37:23.698Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-25T10:54:33.645Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":232,"revision":41,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomPromotion"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"name":"ULTIMATE tickets promo atom - 3NF3lo7axsfEs2vMHQAnEs","variant":"Generic-D","promoHeaderText":"RACE TICKETS - MONACO","promoBodyText":"Don't miss your chance to experience the world's most famous street circuit...","promoImage":[{"url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto/v1749216666/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Racehub%20header%20images%2016x9/Monaco.png","bytes":1396776,"width":1920,"format":"png","height":1080,"metadata":{"aspect_ratio":"16_by_9"},"public_id":"content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Racehub header images 16x9/Monaco","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto/v1749216666/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Racehub%20header%20images%2016x9/Monaco.png","resource_type":"image","access_control":[],"raw_transformation":"t_16by9Centre/f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1749216666/content/dam/fom-website/2018-redesign-assets/Racehub%20header%20images%2016x9/Monaco.png"}],"promoCtaLabel":"BOOK NOW","promoCtaLink":"https://tickets.formula1.com/en/f1-3202-monaco","openNewWindow":false}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"3kifEXjDx6qSOmTIfJCsov","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T09:08:12.931Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:08:12.931Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":4,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomImage"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Image","imageFile":[{"url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto/v1774762016/trackside-images/2026/F1_Grand_Prix_Of_Japan/2268866894.jpg","bytes":1155203,"width":3277,"format":"jpg","height":2184,"metadata":{"caption":"SUZUKA, JAPAN - MARCH 29: Oscar Piastri of Australia driving the (81) McLaren MCL40 Mercedes leads the field away at the start during the F1 Grand Prix of Japan at Suzuka Circuit on March 29, 2026 in Suzuka, Japan. (Photo by Mark Thompson/Getty Images)","alt_text":"SUZUKA, JAPAN - MARCH 29: Oscar Piastri of Australia driving the (81) McLaren MCL40 Mercedes leads"},"public_id":"trackside-images/2026/F1_Grand_Prix_Of_Japan/2268866894","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto/v1774762016/trackside-images/2026/F1_Grand_Prix_Of_Japan/2268866894.jpg","resource_type":"image","access_control":[{"access_type":"anonymous"}],"raw_transformation":"t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1774762016/trackside-images/2026/F1_Grand_Prix_Of_Japan/2268866894.jpg"}],"isLogo":false,"caption":"Power unit performance in 2026 will be monitored across three set periods"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"3mFrXX2FHaESyGiwus8Ys4","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2018-04-24T16:58:50.759Z","updatedAt":"2018-04-24T16:58:50.759Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"channel"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"channelName":"Core Web"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"4DQlu3sQDLvb9i9VP95HkX","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:52.059Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:52.059Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":3,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 5","richTextBlock":"The first period is now formed of the campaign’s opening five rounds (Australia, China, Japan, Miami and Canada), with results to be communicated no later than two weeks after the Canadian Grand Prix.\n\nThe second period will cover Rounds 6-11 (from Monaco to Hungary), while the third period will cover Rounds 12-18 (from the Netherlands to Mexico City).\n\nOnce results have been communicated, power unit manufacturers eligible for ADUO will receive notifications detailing their allowance, and will be able to implement any upgrades as early as the following race. "}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"4RT8I3oKCVNLHtc1xiVHaW","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:42.241Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T11:07:24.904Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":12,"revision":5,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 4","richTextBlock":"### When are the monitoring periods?\n\nUnder Article 4.2 of Appendix C5 of the 2026 F1 Technical Regulations, there are three periods during the 2026 season when power unit manufacturers’ ICE performance will be monitored.\n\nThese three periods were initially listed as Rounds 1-6, 7-12 and 13-18.\n\nHowever, given that the first period – including the Australian, Chinese, Japanese, Bahrain, Saudi Arabian and Miami Grands Prix – was affected by the Sakhir and Jeddah events not taking place, adjustments followed."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"4Z3WmbMNskwsKWg84OwWUG","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2018-04-24T16:58:50.183Z","updatedAt":"2018-04-24T16:58:50.183Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"channel"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"channelName":"Core App"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"55LpDLkFiOGZ7W2byMrm5g","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2024-06-05T16:26:31.045Z","updatedAt":"2025-12-17T13:32:36.280Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":22,"revision":6,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"tag"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"tagName":"2026 regulations","tagDescription":"Current and breaking 2026 regulations F1 stories. Your go-to source for Formula 1 news, podcasts, highlights, results, and expert commentary.","seoTitle":"2026 Regulations, News and Videos | Formula 1","slug":"2026-regulations","tagGroup":"Content - Subject","tagImage":[{"format":"jpg","width":1920,"height":1080,"public_id":"fom-website/2026 regulations/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1765792988/fom-website/2026%20regulations/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.jpg","resource_type":"image","metadata":{},"access_control":[{"access_type":"anonymous"}],"original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1765792988/fom-website/2026%20regulations/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.jpg","url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1765792988/fom-website/2026%20regulations/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.jpg","raw_transformation":"f_auto/q_auto"}]}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"5HjuvBlAV6KU3jYRlLpqmM","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T09:03:45.288Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:03:45.288Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":5,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomImage"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Image","imageFile":[{"url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1773657168/fom-website/Unlocked2026/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.avif","bytes":37086,"width":1920,"format":"avif","height":1080,"metadata":{},"public_id":"fom-website/Unlocked2026/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1773657168/fom-website/Unlocked2026/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.avif","resource_type":"image","access_control":[],"raw_transformation":"f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1773657168/fom-website/Unlocked2026/2026_Explainer_FIA_Rear_3_4_1920x1080.avif"}],"isLogo":false,"caption":"F1 introduced new cars and new power units for the 2026 season"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"5TppklcnBMKv6j5ccPjaaa","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-01-05T09:59:20.312Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-05T09:59:20.312Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"tag"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"tagName":"2026","slug":"2026","tagGroup":"Year"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6IRygB5qY6mpYOp2Kgvou2","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T09:10:18.101Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:10:18.101Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":7,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomImage"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Image","imageFile":[{"url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto/v1678375021/content/dam/fom-website/sutton/2022/Belgium/Saturday/1418400281.jpg","bytes":1059753,"width":5240,"format":"jpg","height":2948,"metadata":{"caption":"SPA, BELGIUM - AUGUST 27: Nikos Tombazis, FIA Single Seater Technical Director attends the Team Principals Press Conference prior to final practice ahead of the F1 Grand Prix of Belgium at Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps on August 27, 2022 in Spa, Belgium. (Photo by Dan Mullan/Getty Images)","alt_text":"SPA, BELGIUM - AUGUST 27: Nikos Tombazis, FIA Single Seater Technical Director attends the Team"},"public_id":"content/dam/fom-website/sutton/2022/Belgium/Saturday/1418400281","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto/v1678375021/content/dam/fom-website/sutton/2022/Belgium/Saturday/1418400281.jpg","resource_type":"image","access_control":[],"raw_transformation":"t_16by9North/f_auto/q_auto","original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1678375021/content/dam/fom-website/sutton/2022/Belgium/Saturday/1418400281.jpg"}],"isLogo":false,"caption":"The FIA’s Tombazis has described ADUO as “a cost cap relief mechanism”"}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6R2KAXCj7KDHit9OS6hUJU","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:25.654Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:25.654Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":3,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 2","richTextBlock":"Various factors are considered, spanning engine speed, input shaft torque and MGU-K (Motor Generator Unit - Kinetic) power, as well as a weighting for power sensitivity on lap time across measured laps.\n\nAs the ADUO assessment focuses on the ICE alone, the FIA admits it is not representative of full power unit performance, given that the ERS (Energy Recovery System) also plays a crucial role in the overall power output."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6YZVPYhcpLrR4UQbUdGYdH","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:18.463Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T11:05:45.674Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":12,"revision":5,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 1","richTextBlock":"__To encourage close competition, F1’s Technical Regulations for 2026 and beyond will allow manufacturers to make updates to their homologated power units – in specific situations – under a new development mechanism. But what is the so-called ‘ADUO’, and how does it work? F1.com presents an all-in-one explainer…__\n\n### What does ‘ADUO’ mean?\n\nFirst up, ‘ADUO’ stands for ‘Additional Development and Upgrade Opportunities’.\n\nDuring specific periods of each F1 season from 2026 to 2030, covering the sport’s [latest power unit cycle](https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/2026-regulations-explained-all-you-need-to-know-about-f1s-new-power-units.14jfv7a36905uDJDdNyfQd), governing body the [FIA](https://www.fia.com/) will monitor each manufacturer’s Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) performance, in turn creating an ‘ICE Performance Index’."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6eaThB0d95QskxG0dorESn","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:37:33.895Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:14:11.502Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":7,"revision":3,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 3","richTextBlock":"### When does ADUO come into play?\n\nIn short, when a power unit manufacturer’s ICE is 2% or more behind the best-performing engine in the Performance Index, ADUO is granted.\n\nAs set out in Article 4.3 of Appendix C5 of the 2026 F1 Technical Regulations, if a manufacturer’s power unit is at least 2% but less than 4% down on the leading ICE, they will be eligible for one additional homologation upgrade in the current season, and an additional upgrade in the following season. \n\nPower unit manufacturers whose Performance Index is at least 4% below the leading ICE will be eligible for two additional upgrades in the current season, and two more during the following season."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6kcKCnijMM4BSWAShaNVid","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T09:07:12.562Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:07:12.562Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":3,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"linkItem"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"name":"Link","title":"Proposals agreed in principle for further evolutionary changes to 2026 regulations","webUrl":"https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/proposals-agreed-in-principle-for-further-evolutionary-changes-to-2026-regulations.2nNLMoEsoD8JYt9rb8zcJB","openInNewTab":false}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6m5BWuGDLxEGhWtxOg0NYt","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T08:22:19.580Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T08:22:19.580Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomVideo"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"name":"Video","videoId":"1858214949253929518","videoMetadata":{"videoId":"1858214949253929518","videoDuration":"11:16","videoDurationInSeconds":676,"caption":"The ultimate guide to the 2026 F1 cars","description":"Sam Collins guides you through every major change in F1's 2026 car and the areas of development to watch out for this season.","publishedAt":"2026-02-26T18:58:12.603Z","thumbnail":{"title":"The ultimate guide to the 2026 F1 cars","path":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/640x360/match/image.jpg","url":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/640x360/match/image.jpg","renditions":{"2col":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/206x116/match/image.jpg","2col-retina":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/412x232/match/image.jpg","3col":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/319x179/match/image.jpg","3col-retina":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/638x359/match/image.jpg","4col":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/432x243/match/image.jpg","4col-retina":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/864x486/match/image.jpg","6col":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/658x370/match/image.jpg","6col-retina":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/1316x740/match/image.jpg","9col":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/997x561/match/image.jpg","9col-retina":"https://d2n9h2wits23hf.cloudfront.net/image/v1/static/6057949432001/eec9c487-26d2-488b-85b6-916588ae16cb/b1f52d04-5224-484a-a491-09e9060840b6/1994x1122/match/image.jpg"}},"url":"/en/video/the-ultimate-guide-to-the-2026-f1-cars.1858214949253929518","sensitive":false,"isProtected":false}}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"6qBZcSw2hYcqZlfI2hONLL","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-15T14:38:02.414Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:17:50.514Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":6,"revision":2,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomRichText"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Text 6","richTextBlock":"### What upgrades can be made?\n\nOnce ADUO comes into play, developments can be applied to a range of power unit components.\n\nAs per the FIA’s list, permitted upgrades include elements of the ICE, engine exhaust system, Turbocharger and waste gate/pop-off, ICE- or exhaust-mounted electrical components and sensors, ERS (and associated cooling systems), the MGU-K, and the car’s Control Electronics, along with hydraulic functions, fluids and ballast.\n\nADUO upgrades are not cumulative within a season, and will only be granted on the first occasion a manufacturer is deemed as eligible to make developments.\n\nMeanwhile, any upgrade not used in a specified season will be forfeited. So, if a manufacturer is granted one upgrade for 2026 and one upgrade for 2027, the 2026 upgrade must be introduced before the end of that season, or it will be forfeited, while the upgrade for 2027 remains valid."}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"bOFt8MODvtMlcBUwlivWO","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T09:06:19.015Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T09:06:19.015Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":3,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"linkItem"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"name":"Link","title":"All you need to know about F1’s new power units","webUrl":"https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/2026-regulations-explained-all-you-need-to-know-about-f1s-new-power-units.14jfv7a36905uDJDdNyfQd","openInNewTab":false}},{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"eqwtu802quzt"}},"id":"gcHCKtbNX629KdCSY2XPu","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-05-18T08:59:03.160Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T08:59:03.160Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":3,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"atomImage"}},"locale":"en"},"fields":{"title":"Header image","imageFile":[{"format":"png","width":1920,"height":1080,"public_id":"fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1","secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png","resource_type":"image","metadata":{},"access_control":[],"bytes":2506639,"original_secure_url":"https://media.formula1.com/image/upload/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png","url":"http://media.formula1.com/image/upload/f_auto/q_auto/v1779094707/fom-website/2026/Miscellaneous/GettyImages-2266409165-1.png","raw_transformation":"f_auto/q_auto"}],"isLogo":false}}]}}
